{
  "$schema": "../scene.schema.json",
  "id": "briarwood",
  "name": "The Briarwood",
  "description": "Bead mw-e25.1 (with mw-e25.22): the Briarwood greybox, 300 x 250 m: a thick old forest of placeholder trunks (pillars) on a flat floor, with the trails of the world map (docs/design/world-map.md). From the town gate at the south end (town-gate, leading back to briar-glen-lane's woodside path, arrive-from-briar-glen-lane) the main trail runs north to the hub clearing (briarwood-hub); from it the trails branch to the Standing Horn clearing (west), the Sleepers' Path corridor (north-west) and on to the priory road, the millpond and drowned lane (north-east), the spur trail to Mooring's Watch (east, ending at moorings-spur, then a gap in the east wall: the moorings-gate transition into the watch, arrive-from-moorings-watch back), the far-bank trail (east) and, off the main trail, the woodcutter's hut (west) and the wolf den hollow (east); the priory road climbs north past the mine road junction and ends at a gap in the north wall: the priory-road-gate transition into Bellwater Priory (arrive-from-bellwater-priory back). Every bible location is a marker spawn named for its world-map node (the rest are planned content beads). Soft boundaries are solid hedges with a bramble gate each (profile bramble-barrier: ivy, so flammable and cuttable): burning or cutting a gate breaks it, which opens the way for walkers and for the navmesh, and the 8 m gates sit between solid, non-burning hedge so a fire stays inside its 12 m neighbourhood. The whole scene is the briarwood region (respawn rules and ambience read it).",
